<section id="external_offers" hidden><h3>Original upstream downloads</h3><div></div></section>
<section id="provided_packages" hidden><h3>Built into Unraid</h3><p>These capabilities are supplied by Unraid and cannot be installed, replaced or removed through NerdTools.</p><ul></ul></section>

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-refresh icon"></i>Update checks</span></div>
<dl>
<dt><label for="update_check_hours">Automatic catalog checks:</label></dt>
<dd>
<select name="update_check_hours" id="update_check_hours">
<option value="0">Disabled</option><option value="1">Hourly</option><option value="6">Every 6 hours</option><option value="12">Every 12 hours</option><option value="24" selected>Daily (default)</option><option value="168">Weekly</option>
</select>
<p>Checks only look for new package versions; they never install anything. Failed checks retry hourly. Saved when you select Apply.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<dl>
<dt><label for="package_release">Package release:</label></dt>
<dd>
<select id="package_release"><option value="latest">Latest compatible release</option></select>
<input id="btnRelease" type="button" value="Use Release">
<p>To roll back, choose an earlier release, select Use Release, then Apply. A chosen release stays pinned until you select Latest compatible release again.</p>
</dd>
</dl>

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-github icon"></i>GitHub access</span></div>
<dl>
<dt><label for="github_token">GitHub token (optional):</label></dt>
<dd>
<input type="password" id="github_token" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Not set">
<input id="btnToken" type="button" value="Save Token"> <input id="btnTokenRemove" type="button" value="Remove Token">
<p>Only needed if checks fail with a GitHub rate-limit error, for example when many devices share one internet connection. Use a fine-grained personal access token with read-only access to public repositories and no other permissions. It is stored on the USB flash drive, so anyone who can read the flash share can read it.</p>
</dd>
</dl>

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-check icon"></i>Apply changes</span></div>
<p>Apply saves your tool selections and the check interval, then installs and removes tools to match.</p>
<input id="btnApply" type="button" value="Apply" disabled>
